'''''Lathyrus annuus''''', the '''annual vetchling''', is a species of annual herb in the family Fabaceae. They are climbers and are associated with freshwater habitat. They have broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 37&nbsp;cm tall.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lathyrus annuus L. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/704231|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Lathyrus annuus (Annual Pea) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/FABC/Lathyrus_annuus.php |access-date=2022-03-05 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref> The species is diploid and has 14 chromosomes (2n=14).<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Gunes |first=Fatma |last2=Ali |first2=Cirpici |date=2008 |title=Karyotype analysis of some Lathyrus L. species (Fabaceae) from the Thrace region (Turkey-in-Europe) |url=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00087114.2008.10589639 |journal=Caryologia |language=en |volume=61 |issue=3 |pages=269–282 |doi=10.1080/00087114.2008.10589639 |issn=0008-7114|doi-access=free }}</ref>

